            "We are creating a murder mystery. A murder mystery needs to have a complex web of evidence for a suspect. When writing a murder mystery, the story should take the point of view of the detective.  Evidence should be collected through investigation, including things like interrogation, hearing conversations, reading past criminal records, looking at mail or trash, and other normal modes of detecting evidence.\n",
